  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Losing your friends in large worlds or trying to meet up with the person you literally just joined off is one of the most frequent annoyances I experience in VRChat.\nAllowing users to ask friends to teleport to them solves this almost entirely for most worlds.\nConsiderations:\n1) Since it requires you being friends, it won't cause annoyance to general public world users and people you don't know.\n2) Most of the time, the friend you joined in the social menu would WANT you to be able to find them.\n3) Getting lost during group meetups and activites hinders the core social experience of VRChat. Users have to resort to communication outside VRC (discord or telegram). As such, the extra UI activity is always less of an intrusion than what players have to resort to now.\n4) This also safely allows players in social instances to respawn if something goes wrong, the world breaks, an avatar is annoying, or they need a break - as they can easily return to the social interaction whenever.\n5) No risk of walking in on private conversation since a confirmation is required.\n___\nThis feature is one of the most commonly utilized among power users I know, before the implementation of EAC, and is a feature that just VASTLY improves the overall social user experience in VRChat.",
